From: SacredTrees <121399723+SacredTrees@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 12:50:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Amiga: file names go to the filing system as ISO 8859-1

WTF hands every path to the filing system as UTF-8 (FileSystem.cpp's
std::filesystem calls, FileSystemPOSIX.cpp's fileSystemRepresentation).
An Amiga file name is ISO 8859-1 bytes. A name with a letter above 127,
"Grün-café.txt", went out as "GrÃ¼n-cafÃ©.txt": no such file. A page that
got that file from its file button saw size 0 and FileReader failed
with NotFoundError, while a file with a plain name read well.

On OS(AMIGA) the four places that cross that border now use ISO 8859-1:
toStdFileSystemPath and fromStdFileSystemPath (FileSystem.cpp),
fileSystemRepresentation and stringFromFileSystemRepresentation
(FileSystemPOSIX.cpp). A character outside ISO 8859-1 becomes "?", as
String::latin1() gives it; such a name cannot be on an Amiga disk.
fileSystemRepresentation keeps its UTF8CString return type (every caller
only passes the bytes on).

Team 2
---
 Source/WTF/wtf/FileSystem.cpp               | 10 ++++++++--
 Source/WTF/wtf/posix/FileSystemPOSIX.cpp    | 12 ++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 20 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Source/WTF/wtf/FileSystem.cpp b/Source/WTF/wtf/FileSystem.cpp
--- a/Source/WTF/wtf/FileSystem.cpp
+++ b/Source/WTF/wtf/FileSystem.cpp
@@ -60,7 +60,11 @@
 
 static std::filesystem::path toStdFileSystemPath(StringView path)
 {
-#if HAVE(MISSING_U8STRING)
+#if OS(AMIGA)
+    // Amiga file names are ISO 8859-1 bytes, not UTF-8.
+    auto latin1 = path.toString().latin1();
+    return std::filesystem::path(std::string(reinterpret_cast<const char*>(latin1.data()), latin1.length()));
+#elif HAVE(MISSING_U8STRING)
 ALLOW_DEPRECATED_DECLARATIONS_BEGIN
     return std::filesystem::u8path(path.utf8().data());
 ALLOW_DEPRECATED_DECLARATIONS_END
@@ -71,7 +75,9 @@
 
 static String fromStdFileSystemPath(const std::filesystem::path& path)
 {
-#if HAVE(MISSING_U8STRING)
+#if OS(AMIGA)
+    return String::fromLatin1(path.string().c_str());
+#elif HAVE(MISSING_U8STRING)
     // FIXME: This uses u8string so how can it be correct inside HAVE(MISSING_U8STRING)?
     return String::fromUTF8(unsafeSpan(path.u8string().c_str()));
 #else
diff --git a/Source/WTF/wtf/posix/FileSystemPOSIX.cpp b/Source/WTF/wtf/posix/FileSystemPOSIX.cpp
--- a/Source/WTF/wtf/posix/FileSystemPOSIX.cpp
+++ b/Source/WTF/wtf/posix/FileSystemPOSIX.cpp
@@ -146,12 +146,24 @@
     if (path.isNull())
         return String();
 
+#if OS(AMIGA)
+    // Amiga file names are ISO 8859-1 bytes, not UTF-8.
+    return String::fromLatin1(reinterpret_cast<const char*>(path.span().data()));
+#else
     return String::fromUTF8(path.span());
+#endif
 }
 
 UTF8CString fileSystemRepresentation(const String& path)
 {
+#if OS(AMIGA)
+    // Amiga file names are ISO 8859-1 bytes, not UTF-8. The type says UTF-8;
+    // the bytes go to the filing system as they are.
+    auto latin1 = path.latin1();
+    return UTF8CString::unsafeFromUTF8(reinterpret_cast<const char*>(latin1.data()));
+#else
     return path.utf8();
+#endif
 }
 #endif
 
